<!--
===============================================================================
Release Files section. `/ship-milestone` reads this block to drive the
per-release version bump. `/setup` populates it from the per-stack default
under `examples/<stack>/release.yml`. Edit the block to match your project's
actual layout — kind: regex is the universal escape hatch for free-form
patterns (e.g., a non-standard README "Latest:" line).

Per-entry keys:
  - path:     repo-relative path
  - kind:     json | toml | yaml | changelog | regex
  - field:    per-kind, and NOT interchangeable (measured against the parser):
              json — any dot-path, array index included:
                     version | package.version | plugins[0].version
              toml — top-level or one-level-dotted only:
                     version | project.version   (plugins[0].version throws at
                     bump time: "bumpToml: could not find [plugins[0]].version")
              yaml — top-level scalar only, NO dots:
                     version                     (project.version is REFUSED at
                     parse time: "yaml kind only supports top-level fields")
  - pattern:  regex with named (?<version>...) group (regex only). Every
              occurrence the pattern matches is rewritten, not just the first.
  - replace:  template using {version} and {codename} placeholders (regex
              only). The template is written LITERALLY — `$&`, `$1` and
              friends land as those characters. Naming {codename} when the
              release supplies none is refused, never written as the literal
              placeholder.
  - optional: bool (default false) — a missing path is `n/a`, not an error,
              and so is a pattern that matches nothing. A NON-optional entry
              still refuses on both.

Full schema + per-kind worked examples: docs/ship-milestone-reference.md.
===============================================================================
-->

## Release Files

```yaml
files:
  - path: package.json
    kind: json
    field: version
  - path: CHANGELOG.md
    kind: changelog
  - path: README.md
    kind: regex
    pattern: 'Latest: \*\*v(?<version>\d+\.\d+\.\d+) — '
    replace: 'Latest: **v{version} — '
    optional: true
```

